arch/s390x, zxfoundation, drivers, build: NNPA facility API, STSI configuration wrapper, and kernel-wide source refactorization

    This change set adds new architecture API surface and reorganizes
    the kernel sources under the directory-scoped zx-discovery
    component model, consolidating module layout across the tree.

    * Architecture API.  Adds the NNPA (Neural Network Processing
      Assist) facility interface for the z16 machine generation — facility
      query, tensor operation functions and parameter block definitions —
      and a typed C++ wrapper for the STSI 15 (current configuration
      level) query, including the configuration topology view.

    * Source refactorization.  Nearly all of arch/s390x and about forty
      percent of zxfoundation are restructured into component-scoped
      layout: each subsystem now carries a manifest, an interface module
      and a separate implementation unit.  The lock/RCU infrastructure
      is consolidated under sync/, the channel subsystem moves under
      io/, and device drivers move under drivers/.  The vendored
      libstdc++ dependency is renamed to zxlibstdc++ and the build glue
      is adjusted accordingly.

    The kernel behaviour is unchanged; this change is structural.